---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What is a Physician Life Care Planner? — MyLifeCarePlanning.com"
  description="A physician life care planner is a board-certified MD or DO who specializes in preparing life care plans for injury, disability, and litigation cases."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-brand-900 text-white">
      <div class="page-container py-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">What is a Physician Life Care Planner?</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-2xl">A board-certified MD or DO who specializes in preparing life care plans for injury and disability cases.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A physician life care planner is a medical doctor (MD or DO) who has completed specialized training in life care planning and holds a recognized certification such as the CLCP (Certified Life Care Planner). They combine their clinical medical expertise with structured planning methodology to produce comprehensive, defensible life care plans.</p>

        <h2>Qualifications</h2>
        <p>Physician life care planners typically hold:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree</li>
          <li>Active state medical license in good standing</li>
          <li>Board certification in a relevant specialty (physical medicine, neurology, orthopedics, etc.)</li>
          <li>Life care planning certification (CLCP, CPLCP, or similar)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What makes a physician LCP different?</h2>
        <p>Unlike nurse or counselor life care planners, a physician has the independent authority to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Diagnose medical conditions independently</li>
          <li>Interpret diagnostic imaging and lab results</li>
          <li>Order and justify future medical treatments</li>
          <li>Serve as a treating or examining physician in addition to a planner</li>
          <li>Provide expert medical testimony at trial</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>When do you need one?</h2>
        <p>You should consider retaining a physician life care planner when the case involves catastrophic injuries such as traumatic brain injury, spinal cord injury, severe burns, amputation, or complex multi-system trauma where the medical complexity of the plan is likely to be challenged at trial.</p>

        <div class="not-prose mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-xl text-center">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-900 mb-2">Find a Physician Life Care Planner Near You</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Search our directory of board-certified MDs and DOs by state.</p>
          <a href="/physician-life-care-planners" class="btn-primary text-sm">Browse by State</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
